# VIC-20 Crunch port

Read **`SPEC.md`** and **`reference/CRUNCH.ASM`** before changing display or the game loop.

## Never

- Change `$9002` column count or `$9003` rows
- Clear `$9002` bit 7 (unexpanded screen is `$1E00` only if bit 7 stays set)
- Use color RAM `$9400` (unexpanded is `$9600`)
- Put code or charset at `$2000+` (no RAM there)
- Point `$9005` at charset before it is filled
- Redefine `$01`–`$1A` (A–Z)
- Invent features not in CRUNCH.ASM (e.g. bombs)
- Collide using screen RAM (use `playfield[]`)
- Poke screen/color outside VBlank

## Always

- Stock screen `$1E00`, charset `$1800`, `$9005=$FE` after fill
- Stub at `$1001` (`SYS 4109`)
- Playfield origin (3,7); tiles `$60`–`$67`
- Loop: input → player/monsters/bullet → wait `$9004` → blit 16×8
- Update `SPEC.md` progress when finishing a milestone
